  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anticipatory Flood Response in Eastern Nepal (EAST)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this anticipatory action project for floods in Nepal is to provide multi-purpose cash, WASH, and child protection services on the basis of early flood warnings to people in the east of Nepal. This UNICEF project provides cash assistance, repairs and installs WASH facilities, provides psychosocial support to children, and disseminates key messages, among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 28,341 people in the Multi-Purpose Cash sector, 7,668 people in the Child Protection sector, and 10,222 people in the WASH sector.</narrative>
  </description>
